 ${python3:Depends},
Description: unified command line for every package manager on the machine
 Meta Package Manager wraps the package managers installed on a machine behind
 one command. It lists, searches, installs, upgrades and removes packages
 through all of them at once, and writes the whole inventory to a single file
 that restores it on another machine.
 .
 The package carries its own Python dependencies in a private directory. It
 adds nothing to the system-wide Python libraries and changes none of them.
